# Every secret and setting this project uses, with where it lives. Values are never stored here.
# For a local build, copy to .env and fill in the "Local builds" section; .env is gitignored.

# ── Local builds ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostHog project token baked into CLI builds (scripts/build-all.ts). Public by design.
# Leave empty to build a CLI that never sends telemetry.
ENVDEN_TELEMETRY_KEY=

# The docs website has its own file: apps/web/.env.example.

# ── GitHub repository variables (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables) ──
# ENVDEN_TELEMETRY_KEY      PostHog token for release builds (envden project, US)
# ENVDEN_GHCR_NAMESPACE     GHCR owner for the Docker image (ghcr.io/<namespace>/envden)

# ── GitHub repository secrets: macOS signing and notarization (docs/releasing.md) ──
# MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12        Developer ID Application certificate with its key, .p12 as base64
# MACOS_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD   Password of that .p12
# APPLE_API_KEY_P8             App Store Connect API key, .p8 as base64 (notarization)
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID             That key's ID
# APPLE_API_ISSUER_ID          That key's issuer ID
# Without MACOS_CERTIFICATE_P12, releases ship ad-hoc signed macOS binaries.

# ── GitHub "release" environment secrets ──
# ENVDEN_HOMEBREW_TAP_KEY   Deploy key with write access to the Homebrew tap repo
# ENVDEN_SCOOP_BUCKET_KEY   Deploy key with write access to the Scoop bucket repo

# ── Provided by GitHub, nothing to set ──
# GITHUB_TOKEN              Releases, GHCR pushes and checks
# npm publishes through trusted publishing (OIDC), so no npm token exists.

# ── Vercel project "envden" (website) ──
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY   PostHog token for cookieless page views, production only
